A||||11||DaRkLoRD||OUCH!||||8||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||03-24-2001||02:44 AM||||Tonight I learned the hard way that I don't remember how to skateboard.. haven't been on a board in almost 8 years.. tonight I was out with some friends who were skateboarding, so I asked if I could try.. first time was fine.. then I tried to go a bit faster, lost my balance and went over on my ankle.. snap..<BR>I've had ice on it all night, yet I still can't move without wincing.. it's swollen and slightly crooked.. I'm gonna ask one of my friends if he'd drive me to the hospital in the morning for some x-rays. Given the choice, however, I'd rather hurt my ankle and have to limp around for a week than smash my tailbone and need one of those rubber donuts. LOL..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Just felt like telling someone.. though it probably looked pretty funny, at least that's what I assume by my drunk friends laughing. (I was the only sober person there) it was even funnier when they tried to help me walk home.. ever see 2 drunk guys try to help steady a person hopping on one foot??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||8
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||03-24-2001||03:35 AM||||I got one for you.<P> A few years ago, I was riding mountain bikes down the rail trail with some friends. (to those who don't know what the Rails to Trails project is. It's where they pave abandoned railroad tracks to get tourists to hike, skate or ride bikes  to lame towns like the one I live in.) At about midnight, I was crossing a road at about 20 mph when all of the sudden, I stop.<BR> While I knew about the barricades that they have keeping the cars from entering the trail, Being midnight, the only available light was the street light about 200 feet away. The light from that, being the orange mercury vapor kind making the grey plastic of the barricade, look just like the cement on the trail. While I didn't crack my skull open, (which would have explained a few things) I did take most of the impact by driving my left knee into the handlebar of the bike. To make matters even worse, I had to pedal my bike 4 miles back to my friends house. That was the ONLY time I was glad I didn't still own my Fiero. I had a van with an auto instead.<P> More on this story in a day or two.....||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||03-24-2001||04:01 AM||||Just another joyful addition to the story.. it's not sprained. it's dislocated.........<P>oww!||||reg||4
Z||000003||LZeitgeist||03-24-2001||07:30 AM||||OWWWWWWWWW!!!!!<P>Damn, now *my* ankle hurts... ack!!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||KRMFiero||03-24-2001||07:45 AM||||::thinks:: I have no clue how to skate board, But i'm pretty good at snow boarding, this winter when i was going up the mountin my board fell off my friends jeep and got ran over by a car. the board is still in usable condition just its all scraped up, would it be possible for me to just bolt on some trucks and use it as a skate bored? hehe that would be funny looking  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000005||KnightRyder31||03-24-2001||10:23 AM||||Man, sorry about about that mis-hap. I've broken an ankle before...martial arts thing.<BR>It really hurt like hell!||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||03-24-2001||01:06 PM||||Ok, I'm back from the hospital.. looks like I'll be immobile for a few days.. not supposed to walk, except with crutches..<P>remind me to avoid skateboards in the future.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnnyK||03-24-2001||01:26 PM||||If you were drunk, you wouldn't have had this problem! Probably wouldn't even had noticed it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Pontiaddict||03-25-2001||04:15 AM||||Of course, if you were drunk, you wouldn't have hurt yourself.<P>Part Two:<P>Okay, I didn't have to go 5 miles back to my friend Bill's house. I could have went 1/2 a mile into town and been at my house. That didn't happen because, 1 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I didn't think it was that bad, and 2 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I felt really stupid and didn't want to go home.<BR>When I get back to Bill's house, I was full of endorphines and laughing like an idiot. I didn't drink that night beause I wanted to retain some credibility. Of course, no one believed me anyway. It's really bad when you are the only sober person in the room, and you are also the only one acting like you just downed a fifth of Jack. When I decided to go home, (about 5:30am) It took me half an hour to get from my van to the house.<P>I'll spare you my pre hospital recovery process. But about 3 weeks later,though I was walkng fine, my knee was still swollen. My mother decided to take me to the redi-med. They proceeded to tell me that I didn't break anything and then stuck a HUGE FREAKIN NEEDLE(!) through one side of my knee, to suck the blood out of the other side. Did it work, NO, my knee was swollen more than before in less than five minutes. Blah, blah, blah. Physical therapy, including those weird elecrical muscle stimulator things. Blah, blah. Lying to physical therapist to get out of it, since it wasn't working. (she, for some reason, reommended more physical therapy.) Eventually, I healed, without their help. So there.<P>But actually dislocating things sucks. Get well soon.||||reg||1
Z||000009||baldlobo||03-25-2001||05:18 AM||||that reminds me of what I did to my knee; I'm riding up a major street heading back to school, half way there I get startled by a person in a big ass GMC Van; so I jamb on my breaks, my thighs hit the handlebars, I fall down and in that process me and the bike rotate some how and I got my knee f*cked up, I'm figuring I can make it home(maybe 1km away) so once I get my bike up I'm riding home and get to a stop light look down at my knee; blood f*cking running down my leg luckly I had a super soaker on me(field day) so I spray my leg off; anyway I had to do that at least three to four more times on the away home.<P>ps I've got some other stories of friends and family of what they've done to themselves.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Standard||03-25-2001||02:06 PM||||ouch, man.<P>I haven't broken or dilocated anything, <B>yet</B>... I'm pretty sure my collarbone is gonna be toast sometime soon.  Worst thing I've done so far was putting two teeth through my upper lip while doing an impression of a lawn dart into the side of a mountain, during my first (and last) downhill mountain bike race.  I crashed, then jumped right back on my bike to finish the race.  Didn't know I hurt anything until I tasted blood in my mouth a little ways down.. hehe I love adrenaline.  After I finished I went down to the medics at the end of the course and they just said "mmmmm... you better go to a hospital.."  Still didn't know I had a hole in my lip until they started stitching it up at the hospital.  Needed 8 stitches.. not too bad.  I have plenty of other scars, too.  Chicks dig 'em  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||03-25-2001||05:50 PM||||I'm happy to report that the swelling is going down, and it doesn't hurt as much today. In retrospect, I probably should have gotten a good nights sleep instead of staying up till 5am with friends watching Indiana Jones movies.. oh well, it was fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||14
